51. Load shedding
This brings us to another useful concept.
Suppose your service receives:
10,000 RPS
but can safely process:
2,000 RPS
You cannot make the other 8,000 magically succeed.
You have two choices:
queue everything
or:
shed load
Load shedding means:
reject excess work early
This is closely related to:
bulkheads
circuit breakers
rate limiting
but conceptually broader.
The goal is:
Preserve system health by refusing work that cannot be safely completed.
________________________________________
52. Brownout / graceful degradation
Suppose Recommendation Service fails.
Instead of:
whole homepage fails
you might do:
homepage
 |
 +--> core content
 |
 +--> recommendations X
Return:
homepage without recommendations
This is graceful degradation.
Now combine:
circuit breaker
+
fallback
+
bulkhead
and the recommendation failure becomes:
recommendation unavailable
rather than:
entire service unavailable
This is the business-level side of resilience.
