67. The "unknown outcome" problem
Suppose:
POST /createOrder
Client times out.
What is the actual state?
Possibilities:
A) B never received request
B) B received but rejected
C) B processed successfully
D) B processed but response was lost
The client cannot know.
Retrying blindly assumes:
A/B
but reality may be:
C/D
Therefore robust distributed systems often need:
idempotency keys
request IDs
deduplication
transaction state queries
Circuit breakers don't solve this.
________________________________________
68. Circuit breaker doesn't mean "don't call B"
It means:
"Based on recent observations, normal calls are currently not admitted."
But you still need:
health probing
recovery
fallback
business policy
And HALF_OPEN is essentially:
controlled experiment
