19. The "narrowest bottleneck" principle
Suppose:
Concurrency limit = 100
HTTP connection pool = 20
Thread pool = 50
What is the actual maximum number of simultaneous HTTP operations?
Approximately:
min(100, 20, 50)
= 20
The narrowest resource becomes the effective bottleneck.
But don't blindly make everything equal.
Different layers have different purposes.
For example:
100 application tasks
        ↓
50 allowed payment operations
        ↓
20 HTTP connections
        ↓
Payment service
Could be perfectly valid if you're deliberately controlling pressure.
The important thing is to understand where the queue forms.
